<header><p class="st-kicker">crusader state · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Tyre</h1><p class="st-meta">1187 CE – 1291 CE (approx.) · capital Tyre</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Crusader lordship of Tyre, saved by Conrad of Montferrat in 1187 and later held by the Montfort family until the end of Outremer.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tyre">Tyre</a>, taken by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusaders</a> with Venetian help in 1124, was part of the royal domain of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a>. In 1187, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin's</a> victory left almost every other town lost, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conrad-of-montferrat">Conrad of Montferrat</a> arrived and held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyre">Tyre</a> against him, ruling it as his own base.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tyre">Tyre</a> was the launching point of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a> and, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a>, the kingdom's main port, with large Venetian and Genoese quarters. In the 1230s-1240s it was a stronghold of Frederick II's officials until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-ibelin">Ibelins</a> took it in 1243. From 1246 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-of-montfort">Philip of Montfort</a> held it as a lordship and built up its trade; he was killed by an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/order-of-assassins">Assassin</a> in 1270.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-montfort">John of Montfort</a> and later heirs held it until 1291, when, after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluks</a> took <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tyre">Tyre</a> without resistance.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="crusader state, 1187 CE – 1291 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M26 24 H74 V52 Q74 74 50 84 Q26 74 26 52 Z"/><path d="M50 24 V84 M26 46 H74"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">crusader state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:83.32%;width:2.07%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1187 CE – 1291 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>crusader state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tyre</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Conrad of Montferrat, Philip of Montfort, John of Montfort</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Latin Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/lebanon">Lebanon</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tyre (crusader)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1239&amp;focus=lordship-of-tyre" aria-label="Lordship of Tyre on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5580 970 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lordship of Tyre lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5900 1226L5908 1277M5900 1226L5815 1335"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5908 1277h0M5815 1335h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5900 1226h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5900 1226h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tyre. <a href="/atlas?year=1239&amp;focus=lordship-of-tyre">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

